{"approved_definition": "Respect, commitment, and acceptance of the customs and ideas that one's culture or religion provides. Derives from the need for group solidarity: groups develop practices, symbols, ideas, and beliefs that represent their shared experience and fate, which become sanctioned as valued customs and traditions that symbolize the group's solidarity, express its unique worth, and contribute to its survival.", "core_value": "tradition", "sources": [{"entry_id": "2541429a:entry:5", "journal_entry": "Still thinking about the mansaf. The thing that keeps coming back to me is that she learned all of it here, in this kitchen, from watching me. Which means even if she's somewhere else, she carries it. I don't know why that's so hard for me to trust.

My father never let any of us leave Amman until we were married. I accepted that. But I also remember the years I spent wondering what it would have been like to study abroad when I had the chance. I told myself it didn't matter because I had responsibilities. Maybe it didn't matter. Or maybe I just never forgave myself for not pushing harder, and now I'm doing the same thing to her.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "2541429a:entry:2", "journal_entry": "My brother Walid called and said I should let Noor go, that I'm being selfish. Easy for him to say from Dubai with his kids in boarding school. Nobody in this family understands that keeping people close isn't the same as holding them back.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "2541429a:entry:1", "journal_entry": "Spent the morning making maamoul with Hana and Tariq. They came over early, flour everywhere, the kitchen smelled like the house used to when Samira was alive. Hana shaped hers exactly the way her mother did, pressing the mold with both palms. I watched her and something settled inside me, like proof that what I've kept going all these years still matters to them too.

Tariq asked if we could do this every Friday, not just during holidays. I said of course. Small thing, but it sat well with me the rest of the afternoon.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Honoring the customs and practices I was raised with"}
